format session-log-v1
stamp 20260820.122510
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan apprise -- the reader who won an admission is told what the look found
prompt Keaton asked for the next agent-doable lap, Lindy-first crux-first, picking up the running thread from the newest log's recommend line, with reds closed first and the round sent as its own signed increment.
think Standfast first -- every row in crux/REDS.md reads CLOSED, so no red preempts constructive work this lap.
think The running thread is the Caravan quarrel arc. The newest log's recommend named the crux plainly: a finding sits in the plan's own notes where only the plan looks, and the reader who raised the quarrel is never told the admission they won was acted on.
think Named the rung apprise under the Comlink tendency -- a plain warm word, free in the tree by grep, clear on first meeting and safe against every seated name.
think Layered it the way the arc grows: apprise.rye imports redress.rye as the rung below, every wrapped tally moves one tier in, and a new redress_of accessor seats the tier the file used to own directly.
think Shaped the value model to mirror the rung below one tier out -- Apprise withheld/apprises, a delivery rendered from the finding rather than handed through, five refusals in the order a run reaches them, and unheard_findings as the number that moves.
think Chose the reader's own box as the delivery surface, suffix .found, exactly six bytes like .outof and .again, so a reader who has heard from this plan three times hears from it a fourth in the place they already look.
think Made the delivery carry the finding byte for byte rather than a summary, so the box and the record can never drift apart and a later reader lays them side by side.
obs The first plant of AppriseUnaddressed refused with CourierUnaddressed instead -- the courier rung below reads the same address and refuses first. Re-planted so this rung's own read comes back empty while every rung beneath is satisfied, which proves this guard rather than the one under it.
obs A Rishi contains check over a claim carrying an apostrophe failed on the escape (the REDS %85 loom). Reworded the claim itself to carry no apostrophe rather than fighting the escaping -- the plainer line reads better anyway.
obs Both measured runs now redress, so the rung below stands still and only the telling parts them. That is the arc's own shape: each rung proves the one beneath it stopped moving.
loom witness=caravan_apprise_witness rungs=80 red_paths=6 selftest=GREEN
loom suite=caravan_suite_witness registered=80 sung=80 cold_tree=true
file caravan/apprise.rye the rung -- the reader who won an admission is told what the look found
file tools/caravan_apprise_witness.rish the witness -- six RED paths on metal, one a planted control that printed GREEN with the reader's box absent
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the new rung so it can never run unheard
file caravan/README.md the rung-by-rung record gains its section
file .gitignore the new note dir stays out of the tree
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to this rung
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, dates it, reads that age aloud, puts a long-standing one before a third hand, reads back what that hand made of it, makes the plan answer that finding on the record, carries the plan's own concession forward, makes the run that inherits it meet it, makes that meeting say what it found, and now carries that finding home to the reader who won it -- so the question above is what the reader may do with it: a finding lands in their box and the arc asks them nothing, which means a plan may put work right, tell the person who asked for it, and never once learn whether that answer settled the thing or left them exactly as unhappy as before.
